# Why Do We Subtract?

This is the most important idea.

Suppose

```
Current player picks 7.
```

Remaining interval lets opponent obtain

```
difference = 5
```

That means

```
Opponent - Current = 5
```

But current already earned

```
+7
```

Overall

```
Current - Opponent

= 7 - 5

= 2
```

So the formula becomes

```
current_gain - opponent_best_difference
```

which is exactly

```python
take_left = piles[l] - maxDiff(l+1,r)
```

